      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping** ([[credential-scoping]]). Here\u0027s how it works:\n\n1. **Local secret loading**: A secrets loader reads the Anthropic API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n\n2. **Child-process injection**: The key is injected only into the environment of the spawned child process (the Ingest agent) immediately before that process starts \u2014 the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated.\n\n3. **Same model for Query agent**: The Query agent receives the credential the same way \u2014 injected into its own environment at spawn, never inherited from or written into the Hub\u0027s process environment.\n\nThis design means a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only in the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5144,
      "output_tokens": 204
    }
